SYNERGETIC COMMUNICATIONS Opened XX/XX/year>XXXX  {$2500.00}

XXXX \ [ Your Full Name ] [ Your Full Address ] [ City, State ZIP Code ] [ Email Address ] [ Phone Number ] Date : [ Insert Today 's Date ] To : XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX. XXXX XXXX XXXX, SC XXXX Subject : Formal Debt Validation and Cease Reporting Demand - FCRA XXXX, XXXX ( a ) ( XXXX ), XXXX XXXX ; FDCPA XXXX ( b ) - Account No. [ Insert Account Number or Reference Number ] To Whom It May Concern, This letter is a formal and lawful demand for full validation and immediate investigation o the account alleged to be associated with my name and credit file under the name of XXXX XXXX XXXX, managed or serviced by XXXX XXXX XXXX. This request is made pursuant to my rights under the Fair Debt Collection Practices Act ( FDCPA ), 15 U.S. CXX/XX/XXXXe XXXX ( b ), and the Fair Credit Reporting Act ( FRA ), 15 U.S. CXX/XX/XXXXe XXXX, XXXX, XXXX, and XXXX. 
Be advised that I am fully aware of my legal rights as a consumer. I am challenging both the legal ownership of this alleged debt and the accuracy of the information being reported to the consumer reporting agencies. I do not acknowledge or accept liability for this debt and hereby request that you immediately cease all collection activities and remove any negative information furnished to XX/XX/XXXX, and XX/XX/XXXXuntil proper and complete valida has been provided and all disputes resolved. 
You are required by federal law to provide the following documentation and information for the account referenced above : XXXX. A copy of the original signed contract or application bearing my signature, establishing a legally binding obligation between myself and the original creditor ; XXXX. The full chain of title and assignment history, including a copy of the bill of sale or transfer agreements ) that clearly outline the assignment from the original creditor to XXXX XXXX XXXX. ThisXX/XX/XXXX Find Similarsgnment and the amount paid for the account ; XXXX. An itemized account history and full breakdown of all transactions, charges, fees and interest applied from the alleged date of default through to the current claimed balance ;

i am stressed out because this company is violating my rights Under 15 U.S.C. 1681s-2 ( a ), data furnishers are required to report only accurate and complete information.

Reporting unverifiable or inaccurate data is a violation of federal law. 

Spring oaks capital LL date opened XXXX XXXX, XXXX  acct # XXXX {$2400.00} XXXX XXXX XXXX date opened XXXX, XXXX  Acct # XXXX {$260.00}

XXXXFormer Account Number: XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXXFormer Service AddressXXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXXDear XXXX Legal Department and Executive Customer RelationsXXXXI am submitting this letter as a formal legal dispute regarding the alleged balance associated with my former XXXX  account.XXXXI dispute this alleged debt in its entirety and do not acknowledge, admit, or agree that I owe the amount claimed.XXXXFor years, I maintained internet service with XXXX and consistently paid my monthly bills. My usage pattern did not materially change, and I understood my service to be a fixed monthly service. At no time was I aware of ongoing additional usage charges that remained unpaidXXXXOn or around XXXX XXXX XXXX I contacted XXXX to cancel my service. During that conversation, I specifically asked the representative to review my account and verify that everything had been completed. After reviewing the account, I was clearly told that "we are all set" and that I should disregard future billing. Based on those representations made by XXXX  I reasonably relied upon those statements and believed that my account had been fully settled and closed.XXXXMonths later, I unexpectedly learned that XXXX claimed I owed additional amounts and that the account had been referred to collectionsXXXXI have reviewed my records and found a serious inconsistency which requires explanationXXXXAccording to my XXXX XXXX statement, XXXX charged an Additional Usage fee of XXXX  for XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXXHowever, the same March statement showsXXXXInternet Usage Credit  Adjustment: XXXXTherefore, the net additional usage charge shown on that statement was zeroXXXXNevertheless, after cancellation of my account, the XXXX XXXX  statement suddenly reinstated these charges and imposed additional late fees, resulting in a balance of approximately XXXXI do not understand why charges that had previously been adjusted and credited by XXXX were later reinstated after my service had already been cancelled.XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX after being contacted by a debt collector, I immediately contacted XXXX again. Between approximately XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX, I spoke with an XXXX representative named XXXXDuring that conversation, I clearly disputed the alleged debt and repeatedly explained that I did not owe the amount claimed. I asked why these charges had never been collected previously, why I had not been notified of any continuing overage charges, and why these charges appeared only after cancellation.XXXXThe representative was unable to provide any explanation and stated that she was merely an agent.XXXXAt no time have I admitted owing this alleged debt.

I have consistently disputed it.XXXXAccordingly, I respectfully demand the following:XXXXA complete copy of my service agreement;
A complete billing history for the account;XXXXDetailed internet usage records supporting all alleged additional usage chargesXXXXDocumentation showing that I agreed to any limited data plan, data cap, overage charges, or additional usage feesXXXXDocumentation explaining why charges that had already been adjusted and credited were later reinstatedXXXXnDocumentation explaining why these charges were not collected monthly if they were legitimate;
Documentation showing any notices allegedly sent to me concerning excess usage or overage charges;XXXXDocumentation explaining why I was informed by your representative during cancellation that "we are all set" and that future bills should be disregarded;XXXXDocumentation explaining why the account was referred to collections before my dispute had been properly investigated;XXXXWritten confirmation that all collection activity has been suspended while this dispute is pending;XXXXImmediate recall of this account from any third-party collection agency;XXXXWritten confirmation that no adverse information has been or will be reported to XXXX XXXX XXXX or any other credit reporting agency while this matter remains disputedXXXXWritten confirmation identifying the collection agency currently handling this account.XXXXIn addition, I have attached supporting documents, including billing statements demonstrating that previously assessed additional usage charges were offset by credits before being reinstated after account closureXXXXI am deeply concerned that inaccurate collection activity or improper credit reporting regarding a disputed and unverified balance may cause unnecessary damage to my credit profile and financial standing.XXXXI respectfully request immediate investigation and a written response.XXXXIf XXXX  is unable to provide documentation supporting these alleged charges, I request that the balance be corrected to zero, all collection activity be withdrawn, and written confirmation be provided that no negative credit reporting has occurred.XXXXhis letter constitutes my formal dispute of the alleged debt.XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX
